-## Not done yet (stage 2)
+## Changed in stage 2 (gate wired and tested)
 
-- Package names, binaries, identifiers and UI strings are still upstream's.
-- SECURITY, SUPPORT and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream.
-- Translated docs, changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
-- Netie gate wiring: Model calls -> OpenVault /v1. Tools -> Cortex tool_runner. Session state persists ids only (crew_checkpoint).
+- Model calls: OpenVault is the one default model endpoint, `${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/v1`
+  (default `http://127.0.0.1:5000`), model `auto`, on every entry point: interactive CLI,
+  oneshot, TUI, messaging gateway, cron, ACP, API server, batch runner, delegation children,
+  MoA presets, the model picker and the setup wizard (default choice "Keep OpenVault"). One
+  URL normaliser (`hermes_constants.normalize_openvault_url`) serves the gate and the model
+  endpoint. Model-provider key fields left `.env.example` and the model section of
+  `cli-config.yaml.example` (its commented custom-provider and auxiliary examples still show
+  `api_key` lines). A user's explicit provider, `base_url` or `HERMES_INFERENCE_PROVIDER`
+  still wins; a `base_url` without a provider logs a WARNING. Error copy names OpenVault,
+  not a vendor.
+- Tools: every tool execution asks OpenVault `POST /api/crew/gate` with ids only
+  (`{kind, id, intent, parent_run_id, child_id, deficit}`, the shape of Netie
+  `scripts/crew_ov_gate.py`) and fails closed with a labelled refusal as the result. Covered:
+  the registry dispatcher, inline, delegate, memory and context-engine tools on both the
+  sequential and concurrent paths, plugin `dispatch_tool` and `call_mcp`, MCP serve
+  `messages_send`, `mini_swe_runner`, the Discord tools, and internal direct callers (web
+  extract and search including `@url:` references, vision including gateway image
+  enrichment, text to speech including auto voice replies and streaming, image generation
+  including the TUI RPC and pet images, speech to text including client-direct voice config
+  and the QQ adapter, voice-live sessions, cron skill loading). Module: `agent/netie_gate.py`.
+- Session record holds ids: the system prompt's sha256, not its body (reused hashes are
+  blanked, an open-time scrub with a marker cleans databases written by older builds);
+  auto-titles off by default; request dumps reduced to digests unless
+  `HERMES_DUMP_REQUESTS` is set; `async_delegations`, gateway prompt pins, the API response
+  store (chains rebuilt from the messages table by row id), the runs idempotency store,
+  delivered replies in the delivery ledger, TUI spawn-tree snapshots and `spawn-ledger.json`
+  keep ids, digests or counters only; CLI input history stays in memory unless
+  `display.persist_input_history` is set; `agent.log` turn lines carry a length and digest
+  unless `HERMES_LOG_USER_TEXT` is set; blanking paths run with SQLite `secure_delete`.
+- Messaging gateways and other leave-machine paths: an OpenVault leave-machine allow is
+  required before any adapter starts, reconnects or serves a profile, and before any
+  standalone send (`send_message`, `hermes send`, cron delivery, the kanban notifier, a2a
+  tools, the Teams pipeline, gateway proxy mode). An adapter refusal is labelled
+  (`netie_leave_machine_refused`) and stays queued for retry; a standalone send returns the
+  labelled refusal as its error; asks run off the event loop.
+- User-visible name and identity: version, help, banner, ACP `/version`, skin, setup,
+  doctor, the WhatsApp reply prefix, the English gateway strings and the agent's own
+  identity ("You are Crew Agent, built on Hermes Agent by Nous Research") use
+  `hermes_constants.PRODUCT_NAME`.
+- Tests: `tests/netie/` (18 files). Two of them are permanent sweeps: a marker sweep over
+  every file and table under `HERMES_HOME`, and a socket-level egress sweep with the gate
+  refusing. `tests/conftest.py` answers the gate `allowed: true` for upstream tests; tests
+  marked `netie_real_gate` keep the real, fail-closed transport.
+
+## Declared, not changed
+
+- The conversation stays in the `state.db` messages table in plain text (TAS-CREW section 6
+  plans session transcripts on Crew disk, hashed; they are not hashed here), and so do these
+  local transcript stores: `cron/output` run archives (`context_from` reads them back),
+  `cache/delegation/live` logs and `subagent-summary` spill files, `agent.log` on failed
+  turns. Data that older builds wrote is labelled with a WARNING, never deleted.
+- Digests are unsalted sha256, so short texts can be guessed by trial.
+- Per-session frozen plugin prompt sections are rebuilt on resume (no stored body).
+- Local, ungated by design: `skill_view` reads, TUI path completion, `bot_mode_dm` local
+  spawns. Not re-asked per delivery: cron's live-adapter lane. Ungated: MCP serve
+  `permissions_respond`, the Discord onboarding token check, the Google Meet realtime CLI.
+- Shared-metrics telemetry is off by default and needs two opt-ins; the update check is
+  content-free. The Anthropic OAuth sanitizer rewrites the identity sentence on that path.
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Package `hermes-agent`, the `hermes` binary, `hermes_cli`/`hermes_state` modules,
+  `HERMES_*` env names and `~/.hermes` are unchanged: they cascade across thousands of
+  files and every install and updater path. Non-English locales, the Ink TUI TypeScript
+  defaults and its history writer (`ui-tui/src/lib/history.ts`), the WhatsApp linked-device
+  name and the release and update banners still say Hermes.
+- OpenVault `POST /api/crew/gate` is not on OpenVault main (Netie TAS-OPENVAULT section 8),
+  so on a real install every tool call and gateway is refused until it lands. Whether
+  OpenVault `/v1` needs a seat token or serves `/v1/models` is not measured; the endpoint
+  carries no key here (`no-key-required`).
+- Subscription-login providers (Codex, Copilot, Qwen OAuth, xAI OAuth and the like) remain
+  selectable by an explicit user choice. DR-0002 rule 6 says they are disabled in a fork.
+- Tool keys for search, image, speech and browser services are still fields in
+  `.env.example`.
+- SECURITY and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream. Translated docs,
+  changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
+- With OpenVault down, a turn fails only after upstream's provider auto-recovery runs out
+  (measured: about 5 minutes for a cron job). A refused loopback OpenVault should fail fast
+  with a message that names it.
