+    layer sets no ``model.provider`` but does set an endpoint (``model.base_url``, or a legacy
+    root ``base_url`` / ``api_base``): the user's endpoint is resolved as upstream does
+    (provider ``custom``), with a WARNING naming it. A ``base_url`` that is the OpenVault /v1
+    URL (after normalisation) is not another endpoint, so the default stands. It is also
+    withheld when the operator set ``HERMES_INFERENCE_PROVIDER`` to a provider other than
+    OpenVault (an explicit opt-in that upstream's ``resolve_requested_provider`` honours when
+    config names no provider); ``auto`` (upstream's no-choice value), ``openvault`` and
+    ``custom:openvault`` keep the default. An explicit
