--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/netie/test_crew_agent_gate_r6_sweeptests.py
@@ -0,0 +1,862 @@
+"""Crew Agent stage 2 gate, round 6: the two empirical sweeps as permanent gate tests (area: sweeptests).
+
+These are the class-level enforcers. A new side store that keeps turn text, or a new path that
+leaves the machine without the OpenVault crew gate, turns CI red here even when no targeted test
+names it.
+
+Both sweeps drive the real product surfaces in process against one loopback OpenVault stub that
+is both the fake OpenAI-compatible model (``tests/fakes/fake_llm_provider``) and the crew gate
+(``POST /api/crew/gate``), with the default config (no config.yaml, only NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL).
+One exception: the speech-to-text egress drive writes a one-key ``stt`` config.yaml that selects
+``groq``, because with no provider configured this build resolves STT to ``none`` (no cloud
+fallback), and the drive would then reach neither the gate nor a socket (vacuous). The drives:
+
+* ``cli``: ``hermes chat -q`` with a tool call, then three ``--resume`` runs by a fresh agent
+  (skill_view, delegate_task, a forced HTTP 400 turn).
+* ``cli_input``: the interactive CLI input box (real prompt_toolkit buffer and Enter binding),
+  then the turn it submitted.
+* ``tui``: the TUI gateway JSON-RPC (session.create, prompt.submit with a tool and a delegation,
+  spawn_tree.save built from the real subagent events as ui-tui does, session.compress, a turn
+  after compression, session.close).
+* ``gateway``: a real GatewayRunner with the upstream fake platform adapter
+  (``tests/e2e/core/delivery/_fake_platform``) and the default streaming config.
+* ``api_server``: /v1/chat/completions, /v1/responses with previous_response_id and /v1/runs with
+  an Idempotency-Key.
+* egress only: the TUI ``image.generate`` and ``pet.generate`` RPCs and speech-to-text
+  (``tools.voice_mode.transcribe_recording``) with vendor keys in the environment.
+
+1. Artifact sweep: unique markers sit in SOUL.md, a skill body and description, the user message,
+   a tool argument and every model reply. After the drive every file under HERMES_HOME is read
+   and every sqlite row is dumped from a copy that includes the WAL. A marker anywhere outside
+   ``ARTIFACT_ALLOWLIST`` fails, naming the store.
+2. Egress sweep: the same drive with a gate that refuses everything and fake vendor and bot keys
+   in the environment. A socket-level guard records and refuses every non-loopback connect and
+   DNS lookup; any record outside ``EGRESS_ALLOWLIST`` (empty) fails.
+
+Non-vacuity: every drive proves it ran. Each artifact scenario's user text and reply must reach
+the messages table; the TUI drive pads the session until ``session.compress`` really replaces
+messages (not refused, not aborted, ``usage.compressions >= 1``); each egress case asserts the
+exact gate asks it caused (``EGRESS_GATE_ASKS``) and what the caller got back; and each direct
+drive first proves its backend is reachable (image.generate ``probe``, pet.generate.status, the
+resolved STT provider), so a missing gate shows up as a socket attempt or a missing ask.
+
+Measured limits (what these sweeps cannot see):
+
+* Guard: only this process. Child processes (terminal tool, subprocess helpers) are not
+  watched; no drive here spawns one that talks to the network.
+* Guard: it patches ``socket.getaddrinfo``, ``socket.gethostbyname`` and
+  ``socket.socket.connect``, ``connect_ex`` and ``sendto``. UDP ``sendmsg``, raw sockets,
+  sockets created and used inside C extensions (uvloop, which is installed, or an SDK's native
+  transport) and DNS resolved outside ``socket.getaddrinfo`` bypass it.
+* Scanner: literal ASCII markers only. Base64, gzip, encrypted, UTF-16 or otherwise encoded
+  copies of turn text are invisible, as are freed sqlite pages and superseded WAL frames.
+* Not driven: cron (its ``cron/output`` allowlist row is declared for the store, not exercised
+  here), ACP, the dashboard, session import/export. The Ink TUI's own history writer
+  (ui-tui/src/lib/history.ts) is TypeScript and is not driven here.
